Clone the repo into Cursor using HTTPS

Go back to the Code tab, click the green Code button, confirm the HTTPS tab is selected (not SSH), and copy the URL starting with [https://github.com/](https://github.com/). Open Cursor (signed into GitHub), press Cmd+Shift+P (Mac) or Ctrl+Shift+P (Windows), type Git: Clone, press Enter, paste the HTTPS link, pick a folder to save it in, and click Open.
Verification: BUILDATHON-2026 appears in Cursor's left Explorer sidebar with README.md and .gitignore, and the bottom-left corner shows main.
